Q: how to return redirects instead of content on path normalized requests? A: <pre><code>server {
    ...

    # block raw URIs that contain explicit dot segments like &quot;/./&quot; or &quot;/../&quot;
    if ($request_uri ~ &quot;(^|/)\.\.(/|$)&quot;) {
        return 404;
    }
    if ($request_uri ~ &quot;(^|/)\.(/|$)&quot;) {
        return 404;
    }

    # standard configuration below...
    location / {
        ...
    }
}
</code></pre>
